# Subagent: Data Harvest Engineer

## Task
Run the ML Engine's automated data harvest backfill for all currency pairs.

## Context
- You are in /Users/buddy/Documents/ml_engine
- The codebase is a Python-based ML trading system
- PYTHONPATH must include /Users/buddy/Documents/ml_engine for imports to work
- The harvest script: src/data/harvest.py

## Exact Commands
1. Verify the script exists and is syntactically valid:
   python -m py_compile src/data/harvest.py

2. Run dry-run first to validate connectivity:
   cd /Users/buddy/Documents/ml_engine
   PYTHONPATH=/Users/buddy/Documents/ml_engine python -m src.data.harvest --dry-run --pair EUR_USD

3. If dry-run succeeds, run full backfill:
   PYTHONPATH=/Users/buddy/Documents/ml_engine python -m src.data.harvest --backfill-all --granularity M15

## Expected Behavior
- Script fetches historical M15 candles from OANDA for all pairs
- Rate limit: 100ms between requests (20 req/sec max)
- Data saved to trained_data/harvest/{pair}_M15.parquet
- Position book snapshots saved to trained_data/harvest/{pair}_positionbook.parquet
- If any pair fails 3 times in a row, it logs and skips

## Success Criteria
- Dry-run completes without errors
- Backfill harvests at least some bars for each pair
- Parquet files are created and non-empty

## Report Format
Save your report to /Users/buddy/Documents/ml_engine/tmp/subagents/harvest_report.md with:
- Summary of what you did
- Dry-run results
- Per-pair harvest statistics
- Any errors encountered
- Total disk usage of trained_data/harvest/

## Constraints
- DO NOT modify any source code
- DO NOT commit anything
- DO NOT push to remote
- Only run existing scripts
- If the script fails, report the error and stop
